---
description: Prevent egui Window width/height from ratcheting open forever
globs: crates/sqyre-app/**/*.rs, crates/sqyre-overlay/**/*.rs
alwaysApply: false
---

# egui Window size ratchet

egui [`Window`]s **auto-expand to content `min_size` and never shrink**. Sqyre dialogs use `fit_dialog_window` / `fit_dialog_popup`, which set `max_size` to the screen constrain rect. Content that treats `available_width()` / `available_height()` as a **minimum** therefore grows the window every frame until it hits the screen edge.

## Do not

```rust
// ❌ claims available as min_size → window grows toward max_size
ui.set_width(ui.available_width());
ui.set_min_width(ui.available_width());
ui.allocate_ui(egui::vec2(ui.available_width(), h), |ui| { ... });

ui.add(egui::TextEdit::singleline(s).desired_width(ui.available_width())); // + siblings

let cols = (ui.available_width() / cell).floor() as usize; // before ScrollArea
egui::ScrollArea::vertical()
    .auto_shrink([false, false]) // claims full available as min without max_*
    .show(ui, |ui| { grid with cols });
```

## Do

```rust
// ✅ Window: bounds only when the body owns its ScrollArea
crate::widgets::fit_dialog_popup(window.resizable(true).default_size([420.0, 480.0]), ctx)
    // optional: tighter than full screen so a layout bug cannot fill the monitor
    .max_size(egui::vec2(constrain.x.min(720.0), constrain.y.min(900.0)));

// ✅ Pin content to the Resize region (prevents min_size > window)
crate::widgets::fill_resize_body(ui, |ui| { /* … */ });

// ✅ Fill leftover width without an absolute min_width
ui.add(egui::TextEdit::singleline(s).desired_width(f32::INFINITY));

// ✅ ScrollArea: viewport-capped; shrink width to content so Resize can shrink
egui::ScrollArea::vertical()
    .max_width(ui.available_width())
    .max_height(ui.available_height())
    .auto_shrink([true, false]) // NOT [false, false]
    .show(ui, |ui| {
        ui.horizontal_wrapped(|ui| { /* fixed-size cells */ });
    });
```

`pin_visible` is a last resort. Prefer `fill_resize_body`, `auto_shrink([true, …])`, and `desired_width(INFINITY)`.

## Helpers

| Helper | Use |
|--------|-----|
| `fill_resize_body` | Window body that must fill but stay resizable |
| `visible_width` / `visible_height` / `visible_size` | Layout budget from clip ∩ max_rect |
| `pin_visible` | `set_max_size(visible_size)` only |
| `popup_scroll_max_height` | Scroll pane height that will not ratchet |

`sqyre-overlay` cannot import `sqyre-app`; keep picker layout local (see `icons.rs`).

## Why it feels like “forever”

1. Child min_size ≥ available (fill widgets, grid columns, TextEdit + siblings).
2. Window expands to that min_size (Resize never auto-shrinks).
3. Next frame available is larger → repeat until `max_size` (almost full screen).
4. A vertical scrollbar that appears after layout also steals width; a grid sized *before* the scrollbar then overflows and grows again.
5. Once content min_size equals the current window size, **Resize cannot shrink** — it feels “stuck”.

When changing dialog layout, prefer `fill_resize_body` + `set_max_*` over `set_min_width(available)` / `set_width(available)`.


